'''''Lotus castellanus,''''' also known as '''Flea Grass''' is a plant in the genus ''[[Lotus (genus)|Lotus]]'' native from Western [[France]] to the Western Mediterranean.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lotus castellanus Boiss. & Reut. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:503538-1 |access-date=2024-08-07 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Lotus castellanus |url=https://www.florandalucia.es/index.php/lotus-castellanus |access-date=2025-01-21 |website=www.florandalucia.es}}</ref>

== Description ==
The flowers of ''Lotus castellanus'' are bright yellow on the top and lighter on the bottom.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lotus castellanus Boiss. & Reut. |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/5356842 |access-date=2024-08-07 |website=www.gbif.org |language=en}}</ref>

The small, clustered, oval leaves of ''Lotus castellanus'' are about four mm with unspaced small hairs.

The flowers have a small tooth towards the top with a small white end.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Occurrence Detail 4145460423 |url=https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/4145460423 |access-date=2024-08-07 |website=www.gbif.org |language=en}}</ref>

== Conservation status ==
''Lotus castellanus'' is not threatened and can be common in some areas.

